{title: Blessed Assurance}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby}
{key: D}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 9/8}
{meta: tune ASSURANCE - Phoebe P. Knapp (1873)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1873, tune 1873: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Blessed as[G]surance, [D]Jesus is mine!
O what a fore[E]taste of [A]glory di[A7]vine!
[D]Heir of sal[G]vation, [D]purchase of God,
[G]Born of His [D]Spirit, [A]washed in His [D]blood.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]This is my story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my Savior [E]all the day [A]long;
[D]This is my [G]story, [D]this is my song,
[G]Praising my [D]Savior [A]all the day [D]long.
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Perfect sub[G]mission, [D]perfect delight,
Visions of rap[E]ture now [A]burst on my [A7]sight;
[D]Angels de[G]scending [D]bring from above
[G]Echoes of [D]mercy, [A]whispers of [D]love.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Perfect sub[G]mission, [D]all is at rest,
I in my Sav[E]ior am [A]happy and [A7]blest,
[D]Watching and [G]waiting, [D]looking above,
[G]Filled with His [D]goodness, [A]lost in His [D]love.
{end_of_verse}
